      ":question/problem": "$\\displaystyle\\int \\left(-x^{2}+5\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}x=$\n\n{{selection}}",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Applying the sum rule, we compute the sum of the integrals of each function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\left(-x^{2}+5\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}x &= \\int \\left(-x^{2}+5\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}x \\\\ &= -\\int x^{2}\\,\\mathrm{d}x+5\\int 1\\,\\mathrm{d}x \\\\ &= -\\frac{x^{2+1}}{(2+1)}+5\\frac{x^{0+1}}{(0+1)}+C \\\\ &= -\\frac{x^{3}}{3}+5x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$",
